#: builder/elements/open-street-map/Globals.php:66
msgid "High-DPI Map Tiles"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/open-street-map/Globals.php:67
msgid ""
"Turn on to request sharper tiles on high-DPI (retina) screens. Only the "
"Carto, Stamen and Mapbox styles serve them; the OpenStreetMap, Topography "
"and Esri styles are unaffected. This doubles the number of tile requests "
"made on high-DPI screens, which counts against the free allowance on your "
"API key."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/open-street-map/Globals.php:73
msgid "MapBox Access Token"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/open-street-map/Globals.php:75
#. translators: %s - Link to documentation.
msgid ""
"Enter your MapBox Access Token to use custom MapBox tiles. For more "
"information please see <a href=\"%s\" target=\"_blank\">MapBox Access Token "
"Guide</a>. Tile requests are made by the visitor's browser, so this token "
"is visible in the page source -- restrict it to your own domain in your "
"MapBox account so it cannot be used elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/open-street-map/Globals.php:81
msgid "Carto API Key"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/open-street-map/Globals.php:83
#. translators: %s - Link to the CARTO API key request form.
msgid ""
"Required for the Carto Light and Carto Dark styles. Carto now stamps \"API "
"Key Required\" across every tile it serves without a key. The key is free "
"and is emailed to you immediately, with no account needed; request one at "
"<a href=\"%s\" target=\"_blank\">Carto Basemaps API Key</a>. Each site "
"needs its own key. Tile requests are made by the visitor's browser, so this "
"key is visible in the page source -- give Carto the domain it will be used "
"on when you request it."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/open-street-map/Globals.php:89
msgid "Stadia Maps API Key"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/open-street-map/Globals.php:91
#. translators: %s - Link to the Stadia Maps signup page.
msgid ""
"Required for the Stamen Toner, Stamen Terrain and Stamen Watercolor styles. "
"Stamen retired its own tile servers and handed these styles to Stadia Maps, "
"which serves them on a free tier. Sign up at <a href=\"%s\" "
"target=\"_blank\">Stadia Maps</a> to get a key. Tile requests are made by "
"the visitor's browser, so this key is visible in the page source -- add "
"your domain to the property allowlist in your Stadia account so it cannot "
"be used elsewhere."
msgstr ""

