#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:121
msgid "Tab Title Alignment"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:122
msgid ""
"Choose how the icon and title are aligned within each tab. \"Space "
"Between\" pushes them to opposite edges. Leave on \"Default\" for centered "
"titles on horizontal tabs and start aligned ones on vertical tabs. Most "
"useful together with a minimum tab width, or with justified tabs."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:144
msgid "Tab Minimum Width"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:145
msgid ""
"Set a minimum width for each tab, so tabs with short titles do not end up "
"narrower than the rest. Tabs still grow past it when the title needs more "
"room. Only applies above the tabs mobile breakpoint. Enter value with unit, "
"ex: 200px. Percentages are not supported. Leave empty to disable."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:166 builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:1075
msgid "Sticky Tabs"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:167
msgid ""
"Turn on to have the tabs navigation stick on scroll. Useful for long "
"content."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:184
msgid "Sticky Tabs Offset"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:185
#: builder/inc/class-fusion-column-element.php:3050
msgid ""
"Controls how far the top of the column is offset from top of viewport when "
"sticky. Use either a unit of measurement, or a CSS selector."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:203
msgid "Update URL On Tab Change"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:204
msgid ""
"Write the selected tab into the page address, so a visitor can copy a link "
"that opens on that tab. The address is replaced rather than added to the "
"browser history, so the back button still leaves the page."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:214
msgid "Content Transition"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:215
msgid ""
"Choose how the tab content changes when a different tab is selected. The "
"outgoing content finishes before the incoming one starts, so the two never "
"overlap."
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:227
msgid "Transition Direction"
msgstr ""

#: builder/elements/tabs/Params.php:228
msgid ""
"Choose which way the incoming content travels, so \"Up\" means it rises "
"into place from below."
msgstr ""

