#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/colors.php:38
msgid "Main Color Palette"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/colors.php:39
msgid ""
"Set your main global color palette. The colors defined here can be used "
"from other global options, from page options and element options. For best "
"results, the 8 colors of the core palette should be set from lightest to "
"darkest. <strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong> If a global color that is used by "
"other options gets deleted, these corresponding options will display a "
"default color instead. Colors are internally stored with a fixed counter. "
"Thus, adding a new color after deleting an old one, will set the same "
"internal name to the new color."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/colors.php:45
msgid "Color Palettes / Color Scheme Mode"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/colors.php:52
msgid ""
"<strong>COLOR MODE:</strong> Define multiple color palettes below. Assign "
"one as the light mode palette and one as the dark mode palette. Use the "
"Default Color Mode to control which palette is active by default, or let "
"the browser preference decide. Visitors can also switch via a Button "
"element connected to the \"Color Mode Toggle\" dynamic data endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/colors.php:57
msgid "Additional Color Palettes"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/colors.php:58
msgid ""
