#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:196
msgid "Optimize Offscreen Rendering"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:197
msgid ""
"When enabled, Containers that are below the fold are only rendered when the "
"visitor scrolls near them. This reduces the amount of work the browser does "
"during the initial load, which can make pages load faster and scroll more "
"smoothly — especially on content-heavy pages. Headers, footers, and the "
"first (few) above-the-fold Containers are automatically exempted so hero "
"content is unaffected. You can override the behaviour per Container in its "
"Extras tab."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:202
msgid "Above The Fold Container Count"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:203
msgid ""
"Number of Containers at the top of the page body that are treated as "
"above-the-fold and therefore kept out of the offscreen-rendering "
"optimization. Increase this if your pages typically start with more than "
"one hero-style Container. Lower it to 0 for page types that start straight "
"into content with no hero. Individual Containers can still override this "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:216
msgid "Emojis Script"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:217
msgid ""
"If you don't use emojis you can improve performance by removing WordPress' "
"emojis script."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:220
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:230
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:302
#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:324
msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:226
msgid "jQuery Migrate Script"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:227
msgid ""
"If you are not using any deprecated jQuery code, you can disable this "
"script to improve performance."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:236
msgid "Load jQuery In Footer"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:237
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to defer loading of jQuery to the footer of the page. This will "
"only take effect if no other jQuery dependent scripts are added to the "
"head. Turning this on can cause JS scripts to break, use with caution."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:242
msgid "Load Stylesheets In Footer"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:243
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to defer loading of the stylesheets to the footer of the page. "
"This improves page load time by making the styles non-render-blocking. "
"Depending on the connection speed, a flash of unstyled content (FOUC) might "
"occur."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:249
msgid ""
"<strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong> .htaccess doesn't exist or it is not "
"writable."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:254
msgid "Enable Compression & Browser Caching"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:255
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to add compression and browser caching rules to the .htaccess "
"file. Brotli is used when the server offers it, with Gzip as the fallback. "
"<strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> This option works only on Apache and LiteSpeed "
"web servers, and needs mod_deflate (or mod_brotli) and mod_expires enabled."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:260
msgid "Enable Video Facade"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:261
msgid ""
"Use video facade in order to load video player only when video is played. "
"<strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> This option is only applied to YouTube and "
"Vimeo elements."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:270
msgid "Clear Object Cache "
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:271
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to clear WP's object cache on post edit, post deletion, and "
"Avada Form Entries page view. This is useful, if your setup or hoster uses "
"persistent object caching, to make sure that queries update when you add or "
"remove posts."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:276
msgid "Persist Query Cache"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:277
msgid ""
"Set to 'on' to store Avada's internal query results in the persistent "
"object cache, instead of only for the duration of each page request. This "
"only has an effect, if your setup or hoster uses persistent object caching. "
"<strong>NOTE:</strong> Some object cache plugins log a notice for these "
"entries."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:282
msgid "Number Of Post Revisions"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:283
msgid ""
"Controls how many revisions WordPress keeps for each post or page. Set to "
"\"-1\" to use the WordPress default (unlimited), \"0\" to disable revisions "
"completely, or any higher number to keep only that many of the most recent "
"revisions. Limiting revisions keeps the database smaller and prevents the "
"post editor from running out of memory on content-heavy pages that have "
"built up a large revision history."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:298
msgid "SVG Media Upload"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:299
msgid ""
"Enable upload of SVG files and improve performance through their smaller "
"image and logo file size."
msgstr ""

