#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:396
msgid "WordPress Big Image Size Threshold"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:397
msgid ""
"Sets the threshold for image height and width, above which WordPress will "
"scale down newly uploaded images to this values as max-width or max-height. "
"Set to \"0\" to disable the threshold completely."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:407
msgid "Image Lazy Loading"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:408
msgid ""
"Choose your preferred lazy loading method for your website's images to "
"improve performance. <strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> The WordPress native "
"method can cause issues with dynamically loaded elements like image "
"carousels."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:418
msgid "Dynamic CSS & JS"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:423
msgid "CSS Compiling Method"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:424
msgid ""
"Select \"File\" mode to compile the dynamic CSS to files (a separate file "
"will be created for each of your pages & posts inside of the "
"uploads/fusion-styles folder), \"Database\" mode to cache the CSS in your "
"database, or select \"Disabled\" to disable."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:434
msgid "Combine Third Party CSS Files"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:435
msgid ""
"Third party CSS files of the selected plugins will be combined into Avada's "
"main stylesheet.<br><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> Enabling this option is not "
"recommended when you are are using third party file combining services, "
"like cache plugins. When this option is changed, Avada Caches have to be "
"reset for changes to apply."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:438
msgid "The Events Calendar"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:450
msgid "Load Media-Queries Files Asynchronously"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:451
msgid ""
"When enabled, the CSS media-queries will be enqueued separately and then "
"loaded asynchronously, improving performance on mobile and desktop."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:462
msgid "Cache Server IP"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:463
msgid ""
"For unique cases where you are using CloudFlare and a cache server, ex: "
"varnish cache. Enter your cache server IP to clear the Global Options "
"dynamic CSS cache. Consult with your server admin for help."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:473
#. translators: %1$s: <code>uploads/fusion-styles</code>. %2$s:
#. <code>uploads/fusion-scripts</code>.
msgid ""
"Resets all Dynamic CSS & Dynamic JS, cleans-up the database and deletes the "
"%1$s and %2$s folders. When resetting the caches on the main site of a "
"multisite installation, caches for all sub-sites will be reset. IMPORTANT "
"NOTE: On large multisite installations with a low PHP timeout setting, "
"bulk-resetting the caches may timeout."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:474
msgid ""
"Resets all Dynamic CSS & Dynamic JS, cleans-up the database and deletes the "
"%1$s and %2$s folders."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:485
msgid ""
"<strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong> JS Compiler is disabled. File does not "
"exist or access is restricted."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:490
msgid "Enable JS Compiler"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:491
msgid ""
"By default all the JavaScript files are combined. Disabling the JS compiler "
"will load non-combined JavaScript files. This will have an impact on the "
"performance of your site."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:496
msgid "Lazy Load Elements"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:497
msgid ""
"By default, only the builder elements actually used on a page are loaded on "
"the front-end. Disable this if you rely heavily on elements added "
"dynamically (e.g. via AJAX) that our scan cannot detect, to load all "
"elements up-front like before."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:502
msgid "Progressive Web App"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:510
#. translators: URL for the plugins page.
msgid ""
"<strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong> To use the Avada PWA feature you need to "
"install and activate the latest version of the PWA plugin. Please <a "
"href=\"%s\">visit the Avada Plugins page</a> to install and activate the "
"plugin and then refresh Global Options to edit the options."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:518
msgid ""
"<strong>IMPORTANT NOTE:</strong> To use the Avada PWA feature your site "
"must use SSL (HTTPS). For more information about the options in this "
"section, please see our <a "
"href=\"https://avada.com/documentation/how-to-use-pwa-progressive-web-apps-"
"with-avada/\" target=\"_blank\">PWA documentation</a> page. To learn more "
"about caching strategies and their use in general you can <a "
"href=\"https://developers.google.com/web/tools/workbox/modules/workbox-"
"strategies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">read this article</a>."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:523
msgid "Enable Progressive Web App"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:524
msgid ""
"Enable this option if you want to enable the Progressive Web App feature "
"and options on your website."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:529
msgid "Cache-First strategy file types"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:530
msgid ""
"File types added in this list will be cached in the browser. Subsequent "
"page requests will use the cached assets. Use this for static assets that "
"don't change like images and fonts."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:539
msgid "Network-First strategy file types"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:540
msgid ""
"File types added in this list will be cached in the browser. Subsequent "
"page requests will first try to get a more recent version of these files "
"from the network, and fallback to the cached files in case the network is "
"unreachable. If your site's content gets updated often we recommend you can "
"use this for your content."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:549
msgid "Stale-While-Revalidating strategy file types"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:550
msgid ""
"Any file types added here will be served with a cache-first strategy, and "
"after the page has been loaded the caches will be updated with more recent "
"versions of the selected file types from the network. Use this for assets "
"that may get updated but having their latest version is not critical."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:559
msgid "App Splash Screen Logo"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:560
msgid ""
"Logo displayed for your website at 512px x 512px when installing as an app. "
"Logo image must be in PNG format."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:568
msgid "App Display Mode"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:569
msgid ""
"If the user installs your site as an app, select how the app will behave. "
"For more information about these options please refer to <a "
"href=\"https://developers.google.com/web/fundamentals/web-app-manifest/#"
"display\" target=\"_blank\">this document.</a>"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:572
msgid "Fullscreen"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:573
msgid "Standalone"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:574
msgid "Minimal UI"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:583
msgid "App Theme Color"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/performance.php:584
msgid ""
"Select a color that will be used for the header of your app, as well as the "
"browser toolbar-color on mobile devices."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/permissions.php:24
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/permissions.php:77
msgid "Roles"
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/permissions.php:78
msgid ""
"Control what each user role can reach and edit across Avada, formerly the "
"Role Manager. “Access” governs the area as a whole; the capabilities beside "
"it narrow what the role can do once inside. Administrators always have full "
"access."
msgstr ""

#: plus/inc/theme-options/sections/privacy.php:245
msgid ""
"The options in this section help you comply more easily with data privacy "
"regulations such as the GDPR. When the \"Privacy Consent\" option is "
